    "done_when": "Defect being repaired: since the request-field merge, ForwardSolveRequest.clip_mode defaults to chord (nova/equilibrium/solve_request.py:491, also the from_policy default at :548), and ForwardProfile._with_source (nova/equilibrium/forward.py:2586) applies it to the operator, so a caller that sets set_support_clip_mode('exact') and then solves through a request built with no mode (for example benchmarks/plasma_cell_terminal_state.py:461 through benchmarks/solovev_certificate.py:2189 _certificate_solve_request) solves in chord. Repair: an omitted clip mode on every request construction route in solve_request.py (the dataclass field, from_defaults, from_policy) resolves to forward_operator.support_clip_mode() when the request is built, so the request, its resolved defaults and its receipt always hold a concrete mode and never None; an explicit mode still wins. Import the getter lazily if a module-level import cycles. The docstring states the mechanism: an omitted mode follows the process mode until every caller passes one. Gate: (1) a new test file tests/test_forward_solve_clip_mode_bridge.py sets the global to exact, builds a request through from_defaults with no mode, solves it on the smallest fixture tests/test_forward_solve_clip_mode_request.py already uses, and asserts that the request, the receipt and the solving operator all carry exact; it also asserts that an explicit chord request under an exact global stays chord, and restores the global in a finally; it fails at the dispatch base with the log kept in the run directory. (2) tests/test_forward_solve_clip_mode_request.py, tests/test_forward_support_clip_mode.py and tests/test_route_solve_requests.py pass with no added failure against the dispatch base. Run the gates in place on this fleet allocation with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, one fresh pytest process per file, logs under the run directory. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. Write the manifest before any long step; its status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
